WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.466
A neural network is a system that learns from examples.

2
00:00:03.466 --> 00:00:06.050
Given an input, it produces a prediction.

3
00:00:06.550 --> 00:00:12.575
Information flows forward through layers of connected nodes, each applying a simple transformation.

4
00:00:13.075 --> 00:00:16.213
The network compares its prediction to the correct answer.

5
00:00:16.213 --> 00:00:19.675
The difference — the loss — tells it how to adjust every weight.

6
00:00:20.175 --> 00:00:23.543
Repeat this across many examples, and the loss falls.

7
00:00:23.543 --> 00:00:24.750
The network learns.
